#   and waf.go: ctl:ruleRemoveTargetById, ByTag and ByMsg, and
#   ctl:ruleRemoveByTag and ByMsg, walked every rule by value on every
#   request, and a target removal then added an entry per selected rule, one
#   allocation each. ctl:ruleRemoveTargetByTag=OWASP_CRS selects every CRS
#   rule, which cost 68 us and 720 allocations a request. A ctl caches the
#   IDs it selects per version of the rule group, which every added or
#   removed rule changes, and the removals share one capped slice: 24 us and
#   118 allocations.
#   Upstream: issue #1848 and PR #1849 (2026-11-08), open at 08aa511.
